1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,459
Some of Egypt’s greatest pharaohs

2
00:00:02,459 --> 00:00:04,815
were discovered together in a secret tomb—

3
00:00:04,815 --> 00:00:06,185
not beneath a pyramid,

4
00:00:06,185 --> 00:00:08,105
but hidden in a cliff.

5
00:00:10,450 --> 00:00:12,145
Their original burial places

6
00:00:12,145 --> 00:00:13,956
had been threatened by thieves.

7
00:00:13,956 --> 00:00:16,104
Gold vanished, coffins were damaged,

8
00:00:16,104 --> 00:00:18,616
and royal mummies were disturbed.

9
00:00:20,450 --> 00:00:22,122
By the Twenty-first Dynasty,

10
00:00:22,122 --> 00:00:23,817
priests of Amun were determined

11
00:00:23,817 --> 00:00:25,245
to rescue the dead rulers

12
00:00:25,245 --> 00:00:27,037
of earlier centuries.

13
00:00:30,450 --> 00:00:32,075
They inspected tombs,

14
00:00:32,075 --> 00:00:33,701
repaired damaged burials,

15
00:00:33,701 --> 00:00:35,883
and carefully rewrapped royal bodies

16
00:00:35,883 --> 00:00:37,594
in fresh linen.

17
00:00:40,450 --> 00:00:42,876
Labels recorded names and transfers.

18
00:00:42,876 --> 00:00:45,036
Some of the mummies were moved several times

19
00:00:45,036 --> 00:00:47,920
before reaching their final hiding place.

20
00:00:50,450 --> 00:00:52,203
Among them were famous rulers,

21
00:00:52,203 --> 00:00:53,712
including Seti the First

22
00:00:53,712 --> 00:00:55,082
and Ramesses the Second,

23
00:00:55,082 --> 00:00:57,780
whose tombs had suffered from robbery.

24
00:01:00,450 --> 00:01:02,575
Their destination was a remote place

25
00:01:02,575 --> 00:01:05,396
among the limestone cliffs of Deir el-Bahari,

26
00:01:05,396 --> 00:01:08,570
across the Nile from ancient Thebes.

27
00:01:10,450 --> 00:01:13,643
The hiding place, now called TT three-twenty,

28
00:01:13,643 --> 00:01:15,129
was also the burial place

29
00:01:15,129 --> 00:01:17,091
of High Priest Pinedjem the Second

30
00:01:17,091 --> 00:01:18,895
and his family.

31
00:01:20,450 --> 00:01:22,575
There, more than fifty people,

32
00:01:22,575 --> 00:01:24,305
including kings, queens,

33
00:01:24,305 --> 00:01:25,767
and other royal figures,

34
00:01:25,767 --> 00:01:29,406
rested among coffins and funerary objects.

35
00:01:30,450 --> 00:01:32,041
Sand and fallen stones

36
00:01:32,041 --> 00:01:33,341
concealed the entrance.

37
00:01:33,341 --> 00:01:35,779
Over many generations, the location slipped

38
00:01:35,779 --> 00:01:37,920
from the wider world’s knowledge.

39
00:01:40,450 --> 00:01:42,250
Then, in the nineteenth century,

40
00:01:42,250 --> 00:01:44,804
members of the local Abd el-Rassul family

41
00:01:44,804 --> 00:01:46,991
discovered the hidden chambers.

42
00:01:50,450 --> 00:01:53,434
According to a famous but uncertain story,

43
00:01:53,434 --> 00:01:55,721
a wandering goat fell into a shaft,

44
00:01:55,721 --> 00:01:58,198
and its owner followed it below.

45
00:02:00,450 --> 00:02:02,784
What he supposedly found was astonishing:

46
00:02:02,784 --> 00:02:05,268
a passage filled with royal coffins,

47
00:02:05,268 --> 00:02:07,242
some marked with the cobra symbols

48
00:02:07,242 --> 00:02:08,755
of kingship.

49
00:02:10,450 --> 00:02:12,191
Objects began circulating

50
00:02:12,191 --> 00:02:13,840
on the antiquities market.

51
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:15,918
Their inscriptions drew suspicion,

52
00:02:15,918 --> 00:02:17,892
and investigators traced the trail

53
00:02:17,892 --> 00:02:19,591
toward the family.

54
00:02:20,450 --> 00:02:21,808
In eighteen eighty-one,

55
00:02:21,808 --> 00:02:23,283
the secret was revealed.

56
00:02:23,283 --> 00:02:26,580
On July sixth, Émile Brugsch and Ahmed Kamal

57
00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:28,941
arrived to secure the tomb.

58
00:02:30,450 --> 00:02:31,657
The contents were cleared

59
00:02:31,657 --> 00:02:33,294
in roughly forty-eight hours.

60
00:02:33,294 --> 00:02:36,185
But poor documentation and damage during removal

61
00:02:36,185 --> 00:02:39,034
would trouble generations of researchers.

62
00:02:40,450 --> 00:02:42,981
In twenty twenty-one, ten royal mummies

63
00:02:42,981 --> 00:02:44,328
discovered in this cache

64
00:02:44,328 --> 00:02:46,917
joined Egypt’s Pharaohs’ Golden Parade

65
00:02:46,917 --> 00:02:49,545
on their journey to a new museum.

66
00:02:50,450 --> 00:02:52,470
The cache preserved a lost chapter

67
00:02:52,470 --> 00:02:53,666
of Egyptian history:

68
00:02:53,666 --> 00:02:55,338
kings rescued from robbers,

69
00:02:55,338 --> 00:02:56,719
concealed for centuries,

70
00:02:56,719 --> 00:02:59,359
and finally brought back into the light.
